            {
                "entry_id": "537f691c-2ea9-3f50-a8de-2ab6f90fced3",
                "word": "armill",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "c2de371f-10ae-4be8-988e-b9b85100fa7f",
                        "entry_id": "537f691c-2ea9-3f50-a8de-2ab6f90fced3",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "armills"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d0d1230f-a6ca-318a-a66b-63da2c33b711",
                        "entry_id": "537f691c-2ea9-3f50-a8de-2ab6f90fced3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A bracelet used in royal coronations, especially that of the monarch of the United Kingdom (symbolically known as a \\\"bracelet of wisdom and sincerity\\\")"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1503c17c-bb5e-4df6-b7ce-f439efebe717",
                                "sense_id": "d0d1230f-a6ca-318a-a66b-63da2c33b711",
                                "text": "The Candidate for membership of Hof, Garth or Hearth shall hold an Armill, or he may touch an unsheathed Sword throughout the ceremony."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5e757da6-2123-3878-bfd2-fb0d093f7e4b",
                        "entry_id": "537f691c-2ea9-3f50-a8de-2ab6f90fced3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A silken stole worn around the neck by royalty."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3234cd67-1dab-49e5-bdf1-1d3b8e061d16",
                                "sense_id": "5e757da6-2123-3878-bfd2-fb0d093f7e4b",
                                "text": "Then the King ariſing, the Dean of Weſtminſter takes the Armill from the Maſter of the great Wardrobe , and putteth it about His Majeſty's Neck[…]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0dba1ac7-a7fd-4f03-9a81-40defc13b6ac",
                                "sense_id": "5e757da6-2123-3878-bfd2-fb0d093f7e4b",
                                "text": "Enough cloth of gold had therefore to be prepared for these purposes, and the Armill is of especial interest, as it introduced all the emblems of the daughter nations for the first time into ceremonial use on such an occasion."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f73424e9-f741-4508-8e69-c21c61011ad0",
                                "sense_id": "5e757da6-2123-3878-bfd2-fb0d093f7e4b",
                                "text": "In 1911 and 1937, the equivalent division was entitled The Investing with the Armill and Royal Robe, and the Delivery of the Orb."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e897a729-c9c0-3ead-88fd-7acea7e6a30a",
                        "entry_id": "537f691c-2ea9-3f50-a8de-2ab6f90fced3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An ancient astronomical instrument, having either one ring placed in the plane of the equator for determining the time of the equinoxes (an equinoctial armil) or two or more rings, one in the plane of the meridian, for observing the solstices (a solstitial armil)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e578e77b-ae8c-4865-86bb-5f0544f95a1e",
                                "sense_id": "e897a729-c9c0-3ead-88fd-7acea7e6a30a",
                                "text": "The Armill, Astrolabe, Dioptra, and Parallactic Instrument of the ancients were some of the instruments thus constructed."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "56ff398d-0040-401c-85da-d658cc87dc2e",
                                "sense_id": "e897a729-c9c0-3ead-88fd-7acea7e6a30a",
                                "text": "This instrument was called an equinoctial armil. Observations taken in this manner must necessarily be very inaccurate, owing to the refraction."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5011a74c-82b6-43f0-b9cf-22178a5910e2",
                                "sense_id": "e897a729-c9c0-3ead-88fd-7acea7e6a30a",
                                "text": "The instruments at this observatory were much admired and included an armillary sphere, a mural quadrant and a solstitial armil."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "af584637-9f63-3ad2-b918-eb7e9dc34531",
                        "entry_id": "537f691c-2ea9-3f50-a8de-2ab6f90fced3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any bracelet or armlet."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    }
